{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I am wearied</b> — He recounts the extent of his illness and his sighings. <b>I weary</b> [ אשחה ]: its meaning is as one who explains <i>השוחה לשחות</i> [the hif'il of the root שוח], and <b>my bed</b> is in construct. The meaning: from whom is my weeping — in the manner of 'no breath remained in me' [i.e., I am utterly exhausted]. And some say: <b>כי אשחה</b> is Aramaic for 'I will bathe.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:09.597922790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}